From 6ceb02d0ff6910de66f915d514fc944e467c38d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Reed <reedswork@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:21:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 53/53] client: Chrome's TLS ClientHello, X25519MLKEM768 and
 brotli certificates

HTTP and WebSocket connections turn on rustls's chrome_hello (patched
rustls), offer Chrome's groups in its order with X25519MLKEM768 first (ring's
X25519 with the RustCrypto ml-kem crate; rustls has the hybrid only on
aws-lc-rs) and decompress brotli certificates, the one compression Chrome
offers.
---
 client/Cargo.toml             |  6 ++-
 client/src/stream_provider.rs | 25 ++++++++++
 client/src/utils/mlkem.rs     | 92 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 client/src/utils/mod.rs       |  2 +
 4 files changed, 124 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 client/src/utils/mlkem.rs

